urname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vecchia</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Wiart</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Woodward</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamaguchi</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The INTERPHONE study: design, epidemiological methods, and description of the study population</article-title><source>Eur J Epidemiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>647</fpage><lpage>664</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Epidemiol||22|647||bib4|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17636416</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chauhan</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Mariampillai</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gajda</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Thansandote</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>McNamee</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of proto-oncogene and heat-shock protein gene expression in human derived cell-lines exposed <italic>in vitro</italic> to an intermittent 1.9&#x02009;GHz pulse-modulated radiofrequency field</article-title><source>Int J Radiat Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>347</fpage><lpage>354</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Radiat Biol||82|347||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16782652</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Christensen</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Schuz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kosteljanetz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Poulsen</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Boice</surname><given-names>JD